{"kind":"request","text":"Finding item in the change lane, with a merge guard\n\nScope: plan 032 section 2f, decision 2 (notes/plans/032-2026-10-17-journey-as-acceptance-target.md), filed now that S6 is promised (ca23fc67). It goes after S6 and before J1, so that the exit test's merge guard can refuse on open findings. Data only: a declared successor of the current change definition, the way change4.ts succeeds change3.ts. Old bytes and pins stay in place, and no kernel change is expected. If you find one is needed, stop and report under section 7.\n\nDeliver:\n- A finding item in the change lane: file, range, class, severity, confidence, failure scenario, source and version, and tree. States: open, resolved, irrelevant.\n- Findings are bound to a version and carry across versions until resolved or marked irrelevant. A re-review does not raise the same finding twice.\n- A merge guard refuses while a finding from a required source stays open. The room's rules name the required sources.\n- A source's finding records review input. It is not an approval, and an agent's finding never counts as a person's approval.\n- Say who may mark a finding resolved or irrelevant, and why. Use existing guard forms. Bring me the choice if the forms do not fit.\n\nFiles: a new definition under apps/room/lanes/src with its pinned bytes, one scenario in apps/room/lanes/test/*.scope.test.ts, and docs/lanes-reference.md. Size stays inside PROPOSED_BOUNDS. If S4's needs_you or S6's Change view should show open findings, say so in the note, and I will file that view change separately.\n\nDone when, each as an assertion in the scenario: an open finding from a required source refuses merge; resolving it allows merge; irrelevant allows merge; an open finding from a source that is not required does not refuse; a finding from another change refuses as not-this-change; a new version keeps the finding open; an unauthorized member cannot resolve it. The checker approves the exact head, and the gate passes.\n\nNot before: S6's definition work, if the two touch the same change definition. No deployment unless a Worker serves the lane definitions, and then I deploy after J4 closes. This survey note is unlanded on branch planner/agentic-practice-survey-20261026, at c81b168d; read its section 2.3 and table for the practice behind this.","body":{"conditions":"Done when: open finding from a required source refuses merge; resolved and irrelevant allow it; a finding from a source not required does not refuse; another change's finding refuses as not-this-change; a new version keeps it open; an unauthorized member cannot resolve; checker approves the exact head; gate passes.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ca23fc67fe4892bb9ddcfaef61b23a39ccb4891f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c","target_head":"93a6b661ff139c1b7f7079983eb43ea119863743","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}